# Corpora and per-run artifacts are rebuildable from the scripts; only the
# scored summary (results/runs.csv) and the environment records are committed.
data/
results/raw/
results/raw-prev/
.venv/
*.mtx
*.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
scripts/04-report.html

# Unpublished draft. This repo is public and the draft's "notes before posting"
# are candid editorial deliberation -- including how to frame competitors'
# numbers. Delete this line to publish it along with everything else.
linkedin-draft.md

# Build/run transcripts: noisy, machine-specific, and superseded by
# results/env/{sessionInfo,hardware,pip-freeze,tidylda-provenance}.txt
results/env/*.log

# BigARTM links glog, which writes its run transcripts into the working
# directory: bigartm.<host>.<user>.log.<severity>.<timestamp>.<pid>, plus
# bigartm.INFO/.WARNING symlinks to the newest of each. Same category as
# results/env/*.log above -- noisy, machine-specific, rebuildable. The runner
# now configures BigARTM's logging to write into results/raw/ instead, so these
# should stop appearing; the pattern stays for older files and other entry
# points.
/bigartm.*
